WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.912
Step 8 is the go or no-go for production.

2
00:00:02.912 --> 00:00:06.134
It starts only when the test
stage's evidence passes,

3
00:00:06.134 --> 00:00:08.756
which the production preflight re-checks;

4
00:00:08.756 --> 00:00:12.127
the test tenant said go and
the rollback was rehearsed;

5
00:00:12.127 --> 00:00:16.396
the policy owner approved the
production records and desired state,

6
00:00:16.396 --> 00:00:18.943
and the change board approved the change;

7
00:00:18.943 --> 00:00:23.213
and CISA telemetry is agreed before
ring 3 retires the VPN's web path.

8
00:00:23.213 --> 00:00:27.837
Step 9 repeats Steps 2 to 7 in
production, one ring at a time.

9
00:00:27.837 --> 00:00:32.812
Its preflight takes the test evidence,
and in the fixture all six checks pass.

10
00:00:32.812 --> 00:00:35.244
For each later ring, change the ring,

11
00:00:35.244 --> 00:00:38.599
use its desired state and
widen the assignments.

12
00:00:38.599 --> 00:00:43.370
Remove a VPN route only after ten
business days with no traffic on it.
